## Delivered

The spec 003 `[CONFIRM]` decision that "Box 54 is required (so the parser
presumes the employer/filing-side copy, not the employee copy)" is superseded.
Both CRA facts were read from "T4 slip - Information for employers" on
canada.ca on 2026-08-03 and are cited in `src/TaxLogicEngine/CLAUDE.md`:

- the payroll account number goes in Box 54 on the employer's own copy and the
  copy sent to the CRA only, and is not entered on the copies given to
  employees, so Box 54 cannot be required;
- indicating employer-offered dental benefits is mandatory for calendar year
  2023 and after, and the relief permitting its omission when code 1 applies
  covers 2023 and 2024 only, so Box 45 remains required for 2025.

`T4SlipParser` no longer requires Box 54, `EmployerAddress`, or
`EmployeeAddress`. Box 12, Box 45, `EmployerName`, `EmployeeName`, and the
per-tax-year rule are unchanged in field name, message, and ordering. No public
type, member, or signature changed; the change is confined to two private
validation methods.

Nothing is invented in place of a removed requirement. An absent Box 54 or
address is carried through as absent — never defaulted, inferred, substituted,
or copied from another field. A present Box 54 still flows to
`T4Slip.EmployerAccountNumber` unchanged.

## Downstream test ownership — scope exception

`tests/CaseProcessing.Tests/Services/T4CaseProcessorTests.cs` is NOT in T01's
file list in `tasks.md`, and AC-45 states the only existing tests modified are
those in `T4SlipParserTests.cs`. That file nevertheless carried
`[InlineData(T4BoxCodes.EmployerAccountNumber, "Box 54")]`, asserting the
processor carries a Box 54 rejection — an error this task removes. Obeying the
file list literally would leave the full suite red and violate the plan's own
rule 6.

EXPLICITLY AUTHORIZED BY THE HUMAN, who directed the downstream change and its
constraints. The obsolete assertion was removed and replaced with stronger
positive coverage; no production CaseProcessing code changed; the floor was
raised, never lowered.

THE PLANNING DOCUMENTS STILL NEED AN AMENDMENT recording that T01 owns this
downstream test file. This task deliberately changed no spec 015 planning
document, so `tasks.md` T01 and AC-45 do not yet reflect what shipped.

## Tests

`tests/TaxLogicEngine.Tests/Services/T4SlipParserEmployeeCopyTests.cs` (new)
pins both directions of the change: valid employee copy without Box 54
accepted; no synthesized account number; blank Box 54 accepted and not
substituted; present Box 54 still surfaced; 2025 without Box 45 still fails;
blank and invalid Box 45 still fail; null/empty/whitespace addresses accepted
and carried through byte-identically; both display names still required; Box 12
still required and its error still never echoes a SIN; 2024/2026/null years
still fail closed with no adjacent fallback; and amount, constrained-value, and
companion rules still fire on an employee copy.

`T4SlipParserTests.cs` — the two superseded rules updated; the all-fields-missing
case now asserts exactly 5 errors and that the three retired rules produce none.

`T4CaseProcessorTests.cs` — Box 54 rejection assertion removed; added positive
proof that an employee copy completes the pipeline with mapped lines, that slip
and mapping still equal the engine's own output, that no account number is
invented and a present one still flows through, that missing addresses reach
processing unsubstituted, that attribution and year coherence hold, and that
Box 12, Box 45, employer name, employee name, and the tax year each still
arrive as the engine's error verbatim and in order, stopping before the
provider.

Mutation-checked: restoring the Box 54 requirement in the parser fails 9 of the
new downstream tests.

## Deliberately not shipped

No extraction module, no document-intelligence provider, no content-read port,
no medical evidence model, no new project, no registration. T01 is only the
parser rule change and its tests.

